**Project Overview**

This project simulates the responsibilities of an IT Administrator managing identities, access permissions, and user lifecycles within a secondary school environment using Microsoft Entra ID (formerly Azure Active Directory).

The objective of this lab was to develop practical cloud administration skills by creating a realistic organisational structure and performing common administrative tasks that are frequently undertaken by IT Support Engineers, Service Desk Analysts, Systems Administrators, and Managed Service Providers (MSPs).

The school environment consists of leadership staff, administrative staff, teachers, and students. Users were organised using security groups and role-based access principles to ensure appropriate access to educational resources and organisational systems.

**Technologies Used**

- Microsoft Azure
- Microsoft Entra ID
- Identity and Access Management (IAM)
- Multi-Factor Authentication (MFA)
- Security Groups
- Role-Based Access Control (RBAC)

